1
00:00:00,234 --> 00:00:03,364
- Sheldon, I know what I'm doing.
- If you knew what you were doing...

2
00:00:03,529 --> 00:00:06,699
(Sheldon:)...there wouldn't be a space toilet
where my coffee table should be.

3
00:00:08,075 --> 00:00:09,655
(Raj:)Howard, wait.

4
00:00:09,827 --> 00:00:13,827
(Raj:)Why don't you use this instead of the PVC
to keep the filter assembly in place?

5
00:00:14,081 --> 00:00:16,831
(Howard:)Because this is not a spare part
from the space station.

6
00:00:17,001 --> 00:00:21,301
(Howard:)This is the thing from the pizza box
that keeps the lid from touching the cheese.

7
00:00:21,881 --> 00:00:25,301
Is that what that's for?
In India, the lid just touches the cheese.

8
00:00:25,468 --> 00:00:28,508
(Raj:)We also have rampant poverty
and periodic outbreaks of cholera...

9
00:00:28,679 --> 00:00:31,219
(Raj:)...so a little cardboard in our cheese
is no biggie.

10
00:00:33,392 --> 00:00:35,232
- Where you going?
- Comic-book store.

11
00:00:35,394 --> 00:00:37,934
(Sheldon:)Oh, an excellent idea.
I could certainly use a break.

12
00:00:38,105 --> 00:00:40,275
- Me too.
- You can go to the comic book store...

13
00:00:40,441 --> 00:00:42,731
(Howard:)...when man can once again
safely poop in space.

14
00:00:43,611 --> 00:00:45,071
(Sheldon:)Why does Leonard get to go?

15
00:00:45,238 --> 00:00:47,488
Because he's upset
over his situation with Penny.

16
00:00:47,657 --> 00:00:51,407
(Leonard:)And if I have to hear about it again,
I'm gonna kick him in his ovaries.

17
00:00:51,994 --> 00:00:54,954
- Thanks for understanding, Howard.
HOWARD: I got your back, sister.

18
00:00:56,249 --> 00:01:01,019
(Howard:)All right, I think we've got a prototype
ready to test. Hand me that Tupperware.

